 forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wyoming remains the most Republican state on the presidential map, and the open-seat nature of the race does little to change that. The baseline partisan lean of roughly R+23 sets the Republican as a heavy favorite, and no general-election polls, expert ratings, or candidate financial data exist to challenge that picture.\n\nHeadlines point to a national environment that has been trending toward Democrats, with voter discontent weighing on the incumbent party. Even so, a swing of that magnitude would need to be several times larger than anything reported to put Wyoming in play. The forecast keeps the Republican safely ahead, with wide uncertainty reflecting the absence of state-specific polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0282, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.025, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0274, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0226, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0279, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0235, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0258, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0202, "margin": -23.0}]}